
# Product Requirements Document (PRD)
# MedSync Analytics Suite

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** January 25, 2026
**Author:** Michael Chen, Product Manager

## 1. Introduction

This document outlines the product requirements for the **MedSync Analytics Suite**, a new add-on module for the MedSync Platform. The Analytics Suite will provide hospital administrators and clinical leaders with actionable insights to improve patient outcomes, reduce costs, and optimize care coordination workflows.

## 2. Problem Statement

Our customers are collecting vast amounts of data through the MedSync Platform, but they lack the tools to easily analyze this data and identify trends. They need a way to measure their performance, identify areas for improvement, and demonstrate the value of their care coordination initiatives.

## 3. Goals and Objectives

- Provide customers with self-service analytics and reporting capabilities.
- Enable customers to track key performance indicators (KPIs) for care coordination.
- Deliver predictive insights to help customers proactively manage patient risk.
- Create a new, high-margin revenue stream for MedSync Health.

## 4. Key Features

### 4.1. Dashboards
- **Pre-built dashboards:** A set of pre-built dashboards for common use cases, such as readmission analysis, length of stay tracking, and care team performance.
- **Customizable dashboards:** The ability for users to create their own dashboards by selecting from a library of widgets.

### 4.2. Reporting
- **Scheduled reports:** The ability to schedule reports to be delivered via email on a daily, weekly, or monthly basis.
- **Ad-hoc reporting:** A flexible reporting tool that allows users to create custom reports with their own filters and dimensions.

### 4.3. Predictive Analytics
- **Predictive Readmission Risk Scoring:** An AI-powered model that identifies patients at high risk for readmission, allowing for early intervention.

## 5. User Stories

- As a hospital administrator, I want to see a high-level overview of our care coordination performance so that I can report on our progress to the executive team.
- As a clinical leader, I want to identify which patient populations are at highest risk for readmission so that I can target our interventions more effectively.
- As a data analyst, I want to be able to create custom reports so that I can answer specific questions about our care coordination data.

## 6. Non-Functional Requirements

- **Performance:** Dashboards and reports should load within 5 seconds.
- **Security:** All data must be handled in a HIPAA-compliant manner.
- **Scalability:** The system must be able to support our entire customer base.

## 7. Release Plan

- **Q1 2026:** Beta release to a small group of customers.
- **Q2 2026:** General availability to all customers.
